{
 "says": "PROTOTYPE of holon:claim payloads (wire leaf holon:claim:v1). Unsigned, unencoded, no signer. Each entry is what a signer would say in one scores row: 'the checks of the declaration's spec held for this claim over these digests'. It does not say the evidence supports the claim. For a price, score 1 says the reading the declaration states (carried or dropped) is what the numbers give. bound and realised are [exponent, mantissa]. A price's standard error and null, the budget, and all prose stay in the declaration. An exact-agreement claim carries no body.",
 "realised": "bound is the bound the claim certifies, the number a reader compares with the consumer's budget; realised is the cost measured on the run cited. In this format a realised certificate has one number, so both carry it (the Constitution session's reading, CIRISAI/CIRISConstitution#215). The budget is never in a row.",
